-
.ai-log/archive/

# The AI-log outbox, not a record. `scripts/submit_log.py` renames it, POSTs it, appends it to
# `.ai-log/archive/YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl` and unlinks it, so on a machine that has just pushed it does not
# exist and everywhere else it holds only what has yet to be sent. Committing it therefore ships a
# queue: whoever pulls gets those entries dropped into their outbox and re-submits them on their next
# push, duplicating them in the graded log. It was committed four times before this rule existed —
# `47dde99` put 156 entries on `main` — and the archive above, which is the actual record, has always
# been ignored. See `.claude/rules/ai-logging.md`.
.ai-log/session.jsonl
.ai-log/session.pending.*.jsonl

# Feedback tracker exports (root only). These are snapshots of a live Google Sheet, so a committed
# copy is stale the moment someone edits a row — and the `Người báo cáo` column is designed to hold
# a person's name, which is not something a public repo should carry even on the days it is blank.
#
# Root-scoped on purpose: eval/ and experiments/ may legitimately commit a CSV of measurements, and
# those are results, not a mirror of somebody else's document.
#
# **What belongs in git is the reading, not the export.** `eval/results/report.md` § 9 is where the
# feedback findings go — counts, the queries that failed, what changed as a result. A tracker with
# 16 rows is evidence; it is only graded if someone writes down what it says.
/*.csv

# Local custom notes (excluded from team repo)
local_notes/

