scratch/

# Local personal workspace (excluded from team repo)
my_workspace/

# Privacy detector weights. Third-party, separately licensed, and fetched per environment — the
# research box needs them, the served image must never contain them. What makes a corpus
# reproducible is the model identity recorded in provenance, not these bytes living in git.
#
# **Leading slash, and it is load-bearing.** Unanchored, `models/` matches a directory of that name
# at *any* depth — including `src/models/`, the Pydantic schemas. Tracked files there were never at
# risk (gitignore does not apply to what git already follows), but a **new** file under `src/models/`
# was silently unstaged: `git add` warns once, `git commit` succeeds, CI passes, and the file is not
# in the repo. Anchoring restricts it to the weights directory at the root, which is the only thing
# the paragraph above is about. Verify with `git check-ignore -v src/models/anything.py`.
/models/

# Personal Claude Code settings — hooks/permissions that are mine, not the team's.
# The team hooks live in .claude/settings.json, which stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Personal Claude memory — auto-loaded beside the tracked CLAUDE.md, but mine alone
# (portfolio/ICM orientation that teammates and non-Claude agents don't need).
CLAUDE.local.md

# Generated from eval/review/band_sample.csv by scripts/band/make_band_review_page.py, and it embeds
# thumbnail paths into an unpublished redaction set. Regenerate it, never commit it.
eval/review/band_sample.html
